Puzzle design references

The authors consulted publicly available puzzle competition archives,
solver write-ups, and authoring guides during design, including material
from the MIT Mystery Hunt community and Puzzled Pint. The paper credits
these research references and describes the design process. Rights in the
referenced source material remain with its respective rights holders.

Bundled third-party resources

Some reference solvers include fonts or glyph data from DejaVu, lexical
resources from CMUdict, Princeton WordNet, Open English WordNet, Wordnik,
wordfreq and other word lists, and components from Tesseract and OR-Tools.
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md indexes the applicable notices. Each bundled
third-party component follows its own terms. The Lost Property vocabulary
is a wordfreq-derived list under CC BY-SA 4.0. Echo Vault's vendored
runtime includes components under Apache-2.0, BSD, MIT, EPL, MPL, Boost,
zlib and bzip2 terms; its adjacent notice identifies the component scope
and how to obtain the corresponding upstream source and patches.

